<div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">24</strong> The tutor recommends against taking Human Physiology because it would not be the best</span><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">A</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t6-l-q24\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"A\"></span><span>time management.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">B</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t6-l-q24\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"B\"></span><span>chance at earning an A.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t6-l-q24\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>topic for a research paper.</span></div></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">25</strong> The student decides to do a dissertation because</span><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">A</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t6-l-q25\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"A\"></span><span>he takes it to boost his GPA.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">B</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t6-l-q25\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"B\"></span><span>he likes to develop more supportive details.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t6-l-q25\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>he wants to conduct more interviews.</span></div></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">26</strong> The student thought the research paper was</span><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">A</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t6-l-q26\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"A\"></span><span>already completed.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">B</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t6-l-q26\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"B\"></span><span>worth finishing.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t6-l-q26\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>too complicated.</span></div></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">27</strong> The method of data collection was</span><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">A</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t6-l-q27\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"A\"></span><span>interviews.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">B</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t6-l-q27\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"B\"></span><span>lab studies.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t6-l-q27\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>questionnaires.</span></div></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":4},{"id":"en-practice-source-2-t6-l-g3-2","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 28-30","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><div class=\"source-section-content-wrapper\"><p>Complete the sentences below.</p><p>Write ONE WORD ONLY for each answer.</p><ul><li>First draft should be finished by the end of <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">28</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t6-l-q28\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>.</li><li>Dissertation should be registered with the <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">29</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t6-l-q29\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> in the Department Office.</li><li>The student can get the relevant database from the <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">30</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t6-l-q30\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> Office.</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":3}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/recent_actual_test_2_academic_listening_test_6_3.mp3"],"order_index":3},{"id":"en-practice-source-2-t6-l-p4","title":"Part 4","part_number":4,"passage_text":"","audio_url":"https://ielts-listening-audio.engnovatemedia.com/3126772-recent_actual_test_2_academic_listening_test_6_4.mp3","question_groups":[{"id":"en-practice-source-2-t6-l-g4-0","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"matching_features","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 31-40","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><div class=\"source-section-content-wrapper\"><p>Complete the notes below.</p><p>Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS for each answer.</p><p class=\"source-transcript-subhead\"><strong>The role of sleep in humans and animals</strong></p><p class=\"source-transcript-subhead\"><strong>Importance of sleep in animals</strong></p><ul><li>Compared to those without food, animals without sleep are more likely to suffer from <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">31</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t6-l-q31\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>.</li><li>Sleep is necessary for all animals, whether they are reptiles, <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">32</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t6-l-q32\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> or fish.</li></ul><p class=\"source-transcript-subhead\"><strong>Differences in animals' sleep and reasons for their ways of resting</strong></p><p><b>Dolphins</b></p><ul><li>swim to the surface when sleeping, because they need to <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">33</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t6-l-q33\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>.</li></ul><p><b>Birds</b></p><ul><li>are constantly <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">34</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t6-l-q34\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> in the presence of numerous predators.</li></ul><p><b>Horses</b></p><ul><li>do most of their sleeping standing up.</li><li>do occasionally take short naps lying down. Lying in one position for a long time could well injure a horse, because their <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">35</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t6-l-q35\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> are delicate.</li></ul><p class=\"source-transcript-subhead\"><strong>Potential problems encountering</strong></p><ul><li>Animals can also have <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">36</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t6-l-q36\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>, the same as humans.</li></ul><p class=\"source-transcript-subhead\"><strong>Importance of sleep in humans</strong></p><ul><li>It helps us to organise our <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">37</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t6-l-q37\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> of the day.</li><li>It plays a key role in <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">38</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t6-l-q38\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>.</li><li>e.g.\n<ul><li>Because of the similar sleeping pattern to that in humans, <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">39</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t6-l-q39\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> are studied in order to increase our knowledge of human physiology.</li><li>Scientists choose to study the <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">40</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t6-l-q40\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> of the fruit fly in order to know the function of the human gene and understand developmental processes in humans.</li></ul></li></ul></div></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":10}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/recent_actual_test_2_academic_listening_test_6_4.mp3"],"order_index":4}],"questions":[{"id":"en-practice-source-2-t6-l-q1","part_id":"en-practice-source-2-t6-l-p1","group_id":"en-practice-source-2-t6-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"matching_features","question_text":"","correct_answer":"B","correct_answer_variants":["B"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[1],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_3126690_1","order_index":1,"points":1,"sourceOptions":[{"value":"A","text":"A. Royal Hotel"},{"value":"B","text":"B. St